# rtk — CLI Proxy for Token Savings

`rtk` is installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/rtk`. Always prefix supported shell commands with `rtk` instead of running them bare.

## Files & Search

```
rtk ls .               # instead of ls -la
rtk read file.py       # instead of cat file.py
rtk grep "pattern" .   # instead of grep / rg
rtk find "*.ts" .      # instead of find
```

## Git

```
rtk git status
rtk git log -n 10
rtk git diff
rtk git add .
rtk git commit -m "msg"
rtk git push / pull
```

## GitHub CLI

```
rtk gh pr list / view 42
rtk gh issue list
rtk gh run list
```

## Tests

```
rtk pytest / rtk go test / rtk cargo test
rtk jest / rtk vitest
rtk err <cmd>          # filter errors only
```

## Build & Lint

```
rtk tsc / rtk lint / rtk cargo build / rtk cargo clippy
rtk ruff check / rtk golangci-lint run
```

## Containers & Cloud

```
rtk docker ps / images / logs <id>
rtk kubectl pods / logs <pod>
rtk aws ec2 describe-instances / rtk aws logs get-log-events
```

## Notes

- Hook auto-rewrites `Shell` tool calls, but prefer explicit `rtk` for clarity and direct control.
- On failure, full unfiltered output is saved to `~/.local/share/rtk/tee/` for inspection.
- Use `rtk gain` to check token savings stats.
